<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    A call takes the floating-point argument register its callee reads on
    entry, when the callee stated no prototype (kuna_calleefloatreads.rs).

    The raw x86-64 image is authored assembly:

      caller:   sub $8,%rsp; movss k,%xmm0; call setf
                pxor %xmm0,%xmm0; cvtsi2ss %edi,%xmm0; call setf
                add $8,%rsp; ret
      pass:     ucomisd one,%xmm0; jbe 1f; jmp half; 1: mulsd one,%xmm0; ret
      leftover: sub $8,%rsp; call getf; lea k,%rdi; mov $0,%eax; call vf; ...
      setf:     movss %xmm0,g; ret
      half:     mulsd one,%xmm0; ret
      getf:     movss g,%xmm0; ret
      vf:       a variadic register-save prologue: test %al,%al; je 2f;
                movaps %xmm0..%xmm7 to the stack; 2: mov (%rdi),%eax; ...

    The pxor heritages all sixteen bytes of xmm0, so with calloverlap off no
    call registers an xmm0 trial and both setf calls print setf(). By default
    (calloverlap auto) each takes the four bytes setf reads. pass forwards
    its own xmm0 to half, which reads it: that trial is the caller's input,
    and in both passes the call passes it. vf tests al and saves every xmm
    register, so the float getf leaves in xmm0 is not passed.

    The fixtures: floatret_wrap_gcc_O2's main calls set_gi_bits(-7.5f) after
    a pxor elsewhere in main. armfloatreturn_armhf.o (hard-float ARM) passes
    a double in d0 to callees with no prototype: twocalls forwards its own d0
    to scale and then a computed d8 * 3.0, a3 and a7 forward theirs to half.
    calleefloatreads_armhf.o (recipe in its .s) is newlib's fmodf shape:
    outer2 forwards s0 and s1 to inner2, which reads s0 and only spills s1,
    so both stay arguments rather than s0 alone.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000" readonly="true"></bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="caller"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x10d4" name="g"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x107a" name="getf"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1071" name="half"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1058" name="k"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1038" name="leftover"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1060" name="one"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1023" name="pass"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1068" name="setf"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1083" name="vf"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option calloverlap off</com>
  <com>lo fu caller</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu pass</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu leftover</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option calloverlap auto</com>
  <com>lo fu caller</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu pass</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu leftover</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/floatret_wrap_gcc_O2</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function main</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/armfloatreturn_armhf.o</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>lo fu twocalls</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu a3</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu a7</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/calleefloatreads_armhf.o</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>lo fu outer2</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #1: off, neither setf call takes xmm0" min="2" max="2">^  setf\(\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #2: by default setf takes the loaded constant" min="1" max="1">^  setf\(dat_1058\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #3: by default setf takes the float converted after the pxor" min="1" max="1">^  setf\(\(float4\)a0\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #4: by default caller takes the int it converts" min="1" max="1">^void caller\(int4 a0\)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #5: both passes forward pass's own xmm0 to half" min="2" max="2">v1 = \(float8\)half\(a0\); // tail-call</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #6: neither pass hands a variadic callee the float getf left in xmm0" min="2" max="2">^  vf\(k\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #7: main takes argc alone" min="1" max="1">^int4 main\(int4 argc\)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #8: main passes -7.5f to set_gi_bits" min="1" max="1">^  set_gi_bits\(dat_2070\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #9: main passes the double it computes to wrapnegd" min="1" max="1">^  wrapnegd\(\(float8\)argc \* dat_2080\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #10: twocalls takes the d0 it forwards" min="1" max="1">^float8 twocalls\(float8 a0\)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #11: twocalls passes its d0 to the first scale" min="1" max="1">^  scale\(a0\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #12: twocalls passes the computed double to the second scale" min="1" max="1">scale\(a0 \* 3\.0\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #13: a3 and a7 forward their d0 to half" min="2" max="2">return \(float8\)half\(a0\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleefloatreads #14: a callee that reads s0 and only spills s1 is passed both" min="1" max="1">inner2\(a0,a1\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
